  "title": "Pohela Boishakh",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**পহেলা বৈশাখ**, the first day of the month of Boishakh, is the Bengali New Year. In Bangladesh it falls on **14 April** every year, and people of every religion celebrate it together. Greet everyone with **শুভ নববর্ষ!** 'Happy New Year!'\n\nTraditions include:\n\n- wearing red and white; many women wear a white sari with a red border\n- streets and courtyards painted with **আলপনা**\n- a village-style **মেলা** (fair) with crafts, toys and snacks\n- in Dhaka, songs at sunrise and a large, colourful street procession with giant masks and figures\n- in towns and cities, a breakfast of **পান্তা ভাত** (rice soaked overnight in water) with fried ইলিশ, which has become a popular custom\n\nMany shopkeepers open a new account book for the year (*halkhata*) and offer sweets to their customers.\n\nThe pattern **শুভ** + occasion is very common: **শুভ নববর্ষ** 'Happy New Year', and later *shubho jonmodin* 'happy birthday'. **শুভ সকাল** 'good morning' exists too, but it's more common in messages than in speech.\n\nEndings: **মেলা** 'fair', **মেলায়** 'to / at the fair': **তুমি কি মেলায় যাবে?** 'Will you go to the fair?'\n\n**Kolkata:** **পয়লা বৈশাখ** (*poyla boishakh*), on 14 or 15 April.",
